message: "If you use notan-route in research, please cite it as below."
title: "notan-route: the order in which a picture's Notan masses lead from one to the next"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Parrish
    given-names: Russell
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9781-7995
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-29
license: MIT
url: https://www.parallaxmetrology.com
repository-code: https://github.com/parallaxmetrology/notan-route
keywords: [notan, composition, painting, value structure, route, transition field, deterministic, image analysis]
abstract: >
  A deterministic route over the light and dark masses of a picture, built on the public
  Notan mass (parallax-notan). From a start, each next mass is chosen by its strength, its
  distance from the current one, and how much mass the straight path between them carries.
  The main readout is the transition field: the route released from every mass, with the
  basins its memoryless successor graph drains into. Ships known-answer scenes and the gates
  the route was locked to, including a kill test against plain strongest-first ranking.
